2026-11-05T08:19:32.887-08:00 [writer] SENT topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="69e65086-2683-4caf-ad6a-216084c7b7a0" plan=["Verify it's CVE-2021-44228 in log4j-core.", "Confirm critical severity (CVSS 10.0).", "Recommend immediate patching to log4j2 2.17.0+."] draft="The Log4Shell vulnerability (CVE-2021-44228) in log4j-core is critical (CVSS 10.0). According to the s0036_rel advisory database (id 20074), this vulnerability affects log4j-core versions >= 2.0-beta9 and < 2.15.0. It enables remote code execution via JNDI lookups in logged strings. The fix was released in log4j2 2.15.0. For immediate security, systems must upgrade to log4j2 2.17.0 or later to resolve this critical vulnerability. Patching to 2.17.0+ is essential as it addresses the Log4Shell flaw while maintaining stability and security. Delaying patching exposes systems to remote code execution risks. Always verify the specific log4j2 version in use before applying updates. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-01 (s0036_rel id 20074): log4j-core affected >= 2.0-beta9, < 2.15.0, severity critical. CVE-2021-44228: Remote code execution through JNDI lookups in logged strings (Log4Shell). Fixed in 2.15.0."
