2026-11-05T08:20:31.998-08:00 [writer] SENT topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="d62ae76a-f339-412e-aa9a-aed2f983065c" plan=["Check security advisories.", "Find fixed version.", "Verify 4.17.11."] draft="The security advisory (s0036_rel id 20075) explicitly states that the template command injection vulnerability (CVE-2021-23337) in lodash is fixed in version **4.17.21**, not 4.17.11. This high-severity vulnerability affects versions prior to 4.17.21. The advisory confirms the fix was implemented in 4.17.21 to resolve command injection via the template function. Version 4.17.11 does not contain this fix and remains vulnerable. Users must upgrade to 4.17.21 or later to mitigate CVE-2021-23337. The advisory database provides no evidence that 4.17.11 addresses this issue; it specifically lists 4.17.21 as the patched version. Always verify fixes against the exact advisory details to avoid security risks. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-02 (s0036_rel id 20075): lodash affected < 4.17.21, severity high. CVE-2021-23337: Command injection through the template function. Fixed in 4.17.21."
