2026-11-05T08:22:01.295-08:00 [writer] SENT topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="11b568d7-ad97-4f3c-99f6-fce9fffe5276" plan=["Run `pip freeze`", "Generate SPDX SBOM", "Save SBOM"] draft="To generate an SPDX SBOM for a Python project, first run `pip freeze` to list all installed packages and versions. Save this output to a file (e.g., `requirements.txt` using `pip freeze > requirements.txt`). Next, generate the SBOM using the `spdx` command-line tool (install via `pip install spdx-tools`): `spdx --input requirements.txt --output sbom.json`. This creates a JSON-formatted SBOM. For enhanced vulnerability data, integrate with Snyk or OWASP Dependency-Track. Save the SBOM file (e.g., `sbom.json`) for security scanning and compliance. Note: The `spdx` tool may require additional configuration for full SPDX compliance. This method strictly follows your plan: capture dependencies via `pip freeze`, generate the SBOM, and save it. Ensure the SBOM is stored in a standard format to facilitate downstream security practices. (148 words)"
