2026-11-05T08:22:12.975-08:00 [writer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_tasks" correlation_id="b0223df0-8b40-47e9-af6a-c58ac08ffc63" partition=0 offset=123 kind="task"
2026-11-05T08:22:20.617-08:00 [writer] SENT topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="b0223df0-8b40-47e9-af6a-c58ac08ffc63" plan=["Identify the vulnerable version range (prior to 2.13.0).", "Confirm the fix is implemented in version 2.13.0.", "Advise users to upgrade to version 2.13.0 or higher."] draft="The vulnerable version range for requests leaking the Proxy-Authorization header (CVE-2023-32681) is **>= 2.3.0 and < 2.31.0**. This vulnerability allows the header to leak during HTTPS redirects. The fix was implemented in **version 2.31.0**, not 2.13.0. The advisory (s0036_rel id 20078) explicitly states the affected range ends at 2.31.0, meaning **version 2.31.0 or higher** resolves the issue. There is no fix in 2.13.0 for this specific vulnerability; the user's plan incorrectly references 2.13.0. Users must upgrade to **requests 2.31.0+** to prevent the Proxy-Authorization leak. Always verify versions against the advisory's exact affected range to avoid confusion. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-05 (s0036_rel id 20078): requests affected >= 2.3.0, < 2.31.0, severity medium. CVE-2023-32681: Proxy-Authorization header leaked to the destination server on HTTPS redirects. Fixed in 2.31.0."
