2026-11-05T08:22:24.865-08:00 [writer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_tasks" correlation_id="248c29a5-3dba-434b-b20c-b2ccb6c0e875" partition=1 offset=121 kind="task"
2026-11-05T08:22:30.701-08:00 [writer] SENT topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="248c29a5-3dba-434b-b20c-b2ccb6c0e875" plan=["Identify the specific security weakness from the Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) list.", "Verify the exact identifier code in the official CWE database.", "Use the identifier in documentation to precisely reference the weakness."] draft="A CWE identifier represents a specific, standardized security weakness defined in the Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) list. It is a unique numerical code (e.g., CWE-122 for \"Improper Limitation of a Buffer\") that precisely references a vulnerability type across the official CWE database (cwe.nist.gov). This identifier enables consistent communication about security flaws without ambiguity. In open-source package vulnerability contexts, tools like Snyk or Dependabot report weaknesses using CWE IDs to categorize risks (e.g., \"CWE-797: Improper Handling of Sensitive Data\"). The identifier directly maps to a documented weakness description, ensuring accurate vulnerability classification and mitigation guidance. Always verify the exact code in the official CWE database to avoid misinterpretation, as this standardization is critical for cross-tool compatibility and effective security patching in open-source ecosystems. (158 words)"
